    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "But, given that at least some nervous systems do give rise to such experience and that the differences between neural networks and non-neural ones (aside from temporal scale) are minimal, it is natural to hypothesize that there is something-it-is-like to being a tissue or organ and making decisions.".
